

Installing or Upgrading the plugin
----------------------------------

1. If you are upgrading Redmine from a version before 6.0, or if
   this is a new installation of the plugin, please see the
   Debian Redmine package maintainer's notes about the new
   mechanism for sharing plugins between multiple Redmine instances
   on the same host.

   In particular, it is necessary to symlink the plugin into the
   /var/... tree for each instance where the plugin should be
   available.

     for INSTANCE in instance1 instance2 instance5 ;
     do
       ln -s /usr/share/redmine/plugins/redmine_agile \
              /var/lib/redmine/${INSTANCE}/plugins/
     done

2. After creating the symlinks, it is necessary to install or
   upgrade the database schema for each instance.  For example,
   for instances named instance1, instance2 and instance5:

     cd /usr/share/redmine
     sudo -u www-data \
       REDMINE_INSTANCE=instance1 \
       RAILS_ENV=production \
       rake redmine:plugins \
       NAME=redmine_agile

     sudo -u www-data \
       REDMINE_INSTANCE=instance2 \
       RAILS_ENV=production \
       rake redmine:plugins \
       NAME=redmine_agile

     sudo -u www-data \
       REDMINE_INSTANCE=instance5 \
       RAILS_ENV=production \
       rake redmine:plugins \
       NAME=redmine_agile

   After each schema update, the script attempts to dump a copy of the schema
   to a file but it is unable to do so due to write permissions.  Nonetheless,
   the schema has been updated correctly and the developers have recommended
   people ignore the error for now:

root@myhost:/usr/share/redmine# sudo -u www-data \
       REDMINE_INSTANCE=instance1 \
       RAILS_ENV=production \
       rake redmine:plugins \
       NAME=redmine_agile
`/var/www` is not writable.
Bundler will use `/tmp/bundlerXXXXXXX' as your home directory temporarily.
** Invoke redmine:plugins (first_time)
.....
** Execute db:schema:dump
rake aborted!
Errno::EACCES: Permission denied @ rb_sysopen - /usr/share/redmine/db/schema.rb (Errno::EACCES)


3. Reconfigure the Redmine package:

     sudo dpkg-reconfigure redmine

4. Restart the Redmine process or the web server hosting Redmine,
   for example:

     systemctl restart apache2

5. In the browser, log in to Redmine and go to

     Administration -> Plugins -> Redmine Agile Plugin -> Configure

   Or browse to https://${YOUR_REDMINE_URL}/settings/plugin/redmine_agile

   If an error page appears, check /var/log/redmine/${INSTANCE}/production.log

6. Select one of your projects in Redmine (or create one), go to

     Settings -> Modules

   Put a tick next to 'Agile' and click 'Save'

7. When you are looking at that project, you should see the Agile tab,
   click the Agile tab to see the agile board.

8. On the main Project list page, click the Agile tab.  The list
   of all issues in all projects appears in an agile / Kanban board.

Dependencies
------------

The ruby-redmine-crm library Gem is now obsolete.  It is superceded by the
ruby-redmineup Gem.  The Debian packaging automatically removes the old
ruby-redmine-crm and installs the new ruby-redmineup when installing
redmine-plugin-agile 1.7.0 or later.

The redmineup Gem library states that it requires ruby-liquid version < 5.0
but redmine_agile plugin seems to work with liquid 5.4.0 installed.
Therefore, the ruby-redmineup library package has been patched to allow
liquid < 6.0

    (legacy) redmine_crm.gemspec (v0.0.63) specifies liquid < 2.6.4

    redmineup.gemspec (v1.1.2) specifies liquid < 5.0

    redmine_agile plugin (Debian package: redmine-plugin-agile)
       no liquid version specified
       Redmineup::Liquid used from
             redmine_agile/lib/redmine_agile/patches/issue_drop_patch.rb

